        "heading_UJ9QYB": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "sub_heading": "NADCO University",
            "heading": "Why Use Paper Tapes?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "rich_text_cstm": "<p>Paper tape—also referred to as masking tape—is a broad category of tapes that includes many water-activated and pressure-sensitive options with paper backing materials (e.g., flatback paper, crepe paper, tissue paper, fish paper, Kraft papers, and clay-coat paper). These tapes are available in numerous variations that differ in color, tensile strength, temperature tolerance, removability, adhesive type, and more—allowing them to support a wide range of industrial and commercial applications.</p><p>Paper tapes offer several benefits that make them a practical and versatile solution, including:</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_cknzkc": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "1. Paper tapes are compatible with many surface materials",
            "content": "<p>Paper tapes adhere well to a variety of substrates, including paper, fabric, wood, metal, corrugated cardboard, plastic, and film. This versatility makes them suitable for applications such as carton packing and sealing, floor marking, color coding, labeling, and masking work.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": true,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_YMyaHz": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "2. Paper tapes are tamper-evident",
            "content": "<p>Many industries use paper tapes as <a href=\"/pages/tamper-evident-labels-for-the-medical-pharmaceutical-industry\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Tamper-Evident Labels for the Medical & Pharmaceutical Industry\">tamper-evident labels</a> to support product safety and security. These tapes help consumers identify if a product has been opened or altered. They are especially common in the <a href=\"/pages/food-beverage-industry\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Food & Beverage Industry\">food, beverage</a>, and pharmaceutical sectors, where tampering poses a risk of illness, contamination, or product damage.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_GUM9Vy": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "3. Paper tapes are highly durable",
            "content": "<p>Paper tapes are engineered with varying adhesive strengths and backing properties to meet different performance requirements. Depending on the grade selected, they can be used for paint masking, packaging reinforcement, heavy-duty sealing, or general-purpose applications. Users can choose the appropriate tensile strength and adhesive level for the job.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_NpGXDy": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "4. Paper tapes are available in a variety of strengths",
            "content": "<p>Paper tapes maintain their integrity in a wide range of environments. They resist changes caused by humidity, temperature shifts, dust, or everyday handling, making them suitable for applications across diverse industrial conditions.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
